# Draft: ntdll: Flag LFH backing blocks correctly in heap_walk_blocks.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11431 state=closed
# HeapWalk() in Wine erroneously reports LFH (Low Fragmentation Heap) internal backing blocks as standard busy blocks (PROCESS_HEAP_ENTRY_BUSY). This causes tools relying on HeapWalk() to misreport false positive memory leaks compared to native Windows behavior.

When a block has the BLOCK_FLAG_LFH flag set, it represents an LFH group region rather than an ordinary user allocation. If it contains active LFH groups, report it with LFH/Region flags instead of a busy block to match Windows behavior and prevent false positives in leak detectors.

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=59938

Signed-off-by: Kyle Yang kyle.chaoxin.yang@gmail.com
